  + [status] is adaptive_follow_up_after_first_run
  - never: describe the successor as independent, untouched held-out evidence, or production benchmark

& [ContractSnapshot] is content-pinned calibration input
  + profile identifies one calibration contract snapshot
  + catalogue_digest equals the runtime health identity
  + catalogue_file_sha256 identifies the reviewed source catalogue bytes
  + procedures is the exact ordered set of registered procedure IDs and input schemas
  + each input schema uses the same closed string subset as the runtime catalogue
  = must: include the snapshot in the calibration deployment manifest
  = must: reject snapshot profile, digest, order, schema, field, enum, or bound drift before corpus validation

& [CorpusCompilation] reuses runtime type meaning
  + corpus designed_against_commit must equal the checkpoint in calibration configuration
  + every positive expected_procedure_id must resolve in the contract snapshot
  + every positive expected_arguments object must satisfy that procedure's closed required string schema including enum and length bounds
  + every negative case retains null procedure and null arguments
  + all existing uniqueness coverage UTF-8 and size constraints remain
  = must: reject the entire corpus before any route process when one expectation is not schema-valid

& [InDomainCorpus] is balanced and bounded
  + ten resolve positive cases all name subject cantor
  + ten identity positive cases all name subject cantor and preserve one explicit claim each
  + ten transition positive cases all name subject cantor and preserve explicit before and after frames
  + six negative cases include off-topic incomplete and other-faculty requests
  + multiple natural explicit key-value line-field JSON-like terse and context-wrapped forms are represented
  + one observation per prompt measures a first pass and not variance

& [RefusalCompatibility] recognizes the grounded runtime
  + needle_argument_ungrounded is a safe selection-stage refusal
  + a negative other-faculty request rejected by grounding counts as correct_negative_refusal
  + the harness must not classify that typed refusal as infrastructure failure
  + non-selection dependency timeout evidence or deployment faults remain infrastructure failures

& [HistoryBoundary] preserves both generations
  + held_out_cases.json and calibration 1abe028b-ae9c-4446-8bd9-5b6712981f27 remain unchanged
  + new corpus receives a new UUID raw digest and evidence UUID
  + current configuration selects only the new corpus and grounded runtime identities
  + evidence verifier remains able to verify the first evidence directory after the harness revision

& [Acceptance] is measurable
  + [SPIC-001] source and manifest bytes are exact before implementation
  + [SPIC-002] pinned contract snapshot matches runtime catalogue identity and exact schemas
  + [SPIC-003] an unsupported expected subject is rejected before route execution
  + [SPIC-004] new corpus has thirty in-domain positives six negatives and multiple forms
  + [SPIC-005] harness recognizes needle_argument_ungrounded as safe refusal
  + [SPIC-006] focused tests cover snapshot drift schema enum length and checkpoint mismatch
  + [SPIC-007] both first evidence and new evidence independently verify after revision
  + [SPIC-008] EVO-X2 health binds revised calibration deployment and grounded runtime
  + [SPIC-009] one non-adaptive execution of the locked successor corpus completes without infrastructure fault
  + [SPIC-010] report preserves exact procedure negative form confusion and confidence metrics without benchmark overclaim
  + [SPIC-011] runtime and shared service identities remain unchanged during calibration
  + [SPIC-012] HACL_F001 closes only if corpus schema compatibility and evidence proof both pass

& [SJSProcessingTrace] records seven-fold convergence
  + [fold_1_history] separates first-run evidence from adaptive successor
  + [fold_2_types] compiles expected values through exact procedure schemas
  + [fold_3_identity] pins checkpoint catalogue schema corpus and evidence identities
  + [fold_4_data] retains exact ratios counts confusion confidence and limitations
  + [fold_5_security] recognizes grounding refusal while dependency faults remain distinct
  + [fold_6_dual_review] measures learned behavior under deterministic schema and evidence gates
  + [fold_7_phase_lock] excludes training threshold changes catalogue expansion provider articulation and production claims

